### V69-D2 (P1) — the opposite direction, from the same line

`Post mortem report for the project` + a truthful answer → **"No change was made — that request did not resolve to an operation I can execute from chat."** **70 of 70** destroyed (14 headlines × 5 truthful answers); #149's zero-modifier pins survive **0/30**. The boundary did not move back, it moved sideways.

**Ruling on the boundary:** do not set the integer to 2 and do not return to position-free — both settings have now shipped a P1 in opposite directions. Distance is the wrong evidence. Requests carry a determiner / identifier / quoted name / imperative frame; headlines are bare noun phrases whose only extra structure is a prepositional phrase. Derive the rule from that, in the one definition.

